# Video settings
Height : 720
Width : 720
FrameRate : 25
LogoPos : BR

# List of positions:
# Takes the form:
#    <alias> is {<location>, <direction>}
# Alias can contain letters, digits and underscores only (no spaces or other symbols).
# Both location and direction are Vector3, printed in the form `(x, y, z)`,
# and are relative to the datacube's normalised position and rotation.
# Positions exported from VR end with a comment saying how they were recorded:
#    #head   - headset position and viewing direction (a camera viewpoint).
#    #cursor - controller position only; direction is always (0, 0, 0),
#              so it is best used as a point to Rotate around.
# These tags are just comments and have no effect on the video.

center is {(0,0,0), (0,0,0)} #cursor
front is {(0, 0, -2), (0, 0, 0)} #head

# Script:
# Accepted commands (see documentation for details):
#    - Start at <alias>
#    - Wait <n> seconds
#    - Move in <METHOD> to <alias> over <n> seconds
#        - Methods allowed: (LINE, ARC)
#    - Rotate around <alias> <n> times [turn <n> seconds] [orbit <n> seconds]
#        - turn: seconds spent turning to face <alias> first (default 5)
#        - orbit: seconds for each full orbit (default 10)

Start at front

Wait 0.5 seconds

#Simple turntable using Rotate
Rotate around center 1 times turn 0 seconds orbit 8 seconds

Wait 1 seconds
